    {
      "id": "iYcakU9T5Tv_aUFX-kL8I",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 171,
      "y": 724,
      "width": 577,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 314992309,
      "version": 357,
      "versionNonce": 666672245,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785391137657,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Method overloading is a concept in which In same scope \nmultiple methods are created with same name .\n\n2. But they must be different in terms of arguement.\n\nDiffrenet can be of three types :\n\n1. No. of arguements.\n\n2. Order of arguements.\n\n3. data types of arguements.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Method overloading is a concept in which In same scope \nmultiple methods are created with same name .\n\n2. But they must be different in terms of arguement.\n\nDiffrenet can be of three types :\n\n1. No. of arguements.\n\n2. Order of arguements.\n\n3. data types of arguements.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
