      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785394019553,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Means In one class we are going to provide multiple \nconstructor.\n\n2. Every Constructor must be different in terms of arguement.\n\n3. When object created java will call the constructor which closely \nmatches the exact parameter type.\n\nBenefits is that programmer can create object in multiple ways.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Means In one class we are going to provide multiple \nconstructor.\n\n2. Every Constructor must be different in terms of arguement.\n\n3. When object created java will call the constructor which closely \nmatches the exact parameter type.\n\nBenefits is that programmer can create object in multiple ways.",
